1
00:00:00,802 --> 00:00:05,530
EveryMind trains Maryland students, school staff and families to know when to use 988.

2
00:00:05,530 --> 00:00:08,334
Every session ends with a survey, but a spreadsheet

3
00:00:08,334 --> 00:00:10,808
of answers doesn't tell staff what to change.

4
00:00:11,266 --> 00:00:12,452
Our tool is a website.

5
00:00:12,452 --> 00:00:15,471
Open the link and the dashboard is ready: no install and

6
00:00:15,471 --> 00:00:18,544
no login, and every number shows how many people it rests

7
00:00:18,543 --> 00:00:18,705
on.

8
00:00:19,161 --> 00:00:21,072
Here are 1,299 responses.

9
00:00:21,072 --> 00:00:24,894
After training, 92% say they know when to use 988.

10
00:00:24,894 --> 00:00:29,328
The biggest jump is describing 988: 46% before, 90% after.

11
00:00:29,328 --> 00:00:35,749
The "before" was asked afterward, so the dashboard flags that gap as an upper bound.

12
00:00:36,209 --> 00:00:38,083
Pick any measure and any group.

13
00:00:38,083 --> 00:00:41,469
Every bar shows how many people it rests on and a likely

14
00:00:41,469 --> 00:00:45,157
range, and groups under ten people are hidden, never guessed.

15
00:00:45,156 --> 00:00:48,844
Students rate the training 7.2 out of ten; school staff, 9.5.

16
00:00:48,844 --> 00:00:52,532
The ranges don't overlap, so that gap is worth a closer look.

17
00:00:52,991 --> 00:00:55,047
Comments are coded into themes.

18
00:00:55,047 --> 00:01:00,485
What 988 is was the most valued lesson, in 47% of comments, and 35% of improvement

19
00:01:00,484 --> 00:01:05,590
comments were really questions about 988, a sign to leave time for questions.

20
00:01:06,045 --> 00:01:11,208
Our top recommendation: only 293 people answered whether they would actually call 988.

21
00:01:11,208 --> 00:01:14,690
Make that question required, and add a short survey at the

22
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:18,232
start of each session, so next season measures real change.

23
00:01:18,689 --> 00:01:21,590
Next month, click Update and drop in the new export.

24
00:01:21,590 --> 00:01:23,376
Here we use a made-up test file.

25
00:01:23,376 --> 00:01:28,286
Every number is recalculated inside the browser, and the file never leaves the computer.

26
00:01:28,749 --> 00:01:33,162
Counties or answer labels the tool doesn't recognize are flagged here, never dropped.

27
00:01:33,162 --> 00:01:36,484
Download the new dashboard, and share it with staff and funders.
